%T A402676 81,84,90,92,98,99,100,108,112,116,117,121,124,126,132,140,147,148,
%U A402676 150,153,156,162,164,169,171,172,175,176,180,188,192,196,198,200,204,207,208
%N A402676 Numbers whose prime factorization contains one or more even exponents, all of which are equal.
%C A402676 Subsequence of A072587 and first differs from it at n = 40: A072587(40) = 144 is not a term in this sequence.
%C A402676 First differs from its subsequence A384519 at n = 20: a(20) = 72 is not a term in A384519.
%C A402676 Differs from A240112 by having the terms 72, 200, 360, ..., and not having the terms 144, 324, 400, ... .
%C A402676 Differs from A368714 by having the terms 72, 108, 200, ..., and not having the terms 1, 144, 324, 400, ... .
%C A402676 Differs from A398820 by having the terms 72, 108, 200, ..., and not having the terms 144, 324, 400, ... .
%C A402676 Numbers whose largest unitary divisor that is a square (A350388) is greater than 1 and is equal to an even power of a squarefree number (A384517).
%C A402676 Numbers of the form m * s^k, where m is an exponentially odd number, s > 1 is a squarefree number coprime to m, and k >= 2 is even.
%C A402676 The asymptotic density of this sequence is d * Sum_{k>=1} (Product_{p prime} (1 + (p^2-1)/(p^(2*k) * (p^2 + p - 1))) - 1) = 0.28725243251811315438..., where d = A065463 is the asymptotic density of the exponentially odd numbers.
%H A402676 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A402676/b402676.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A402676 <a href="/index/Eu#epf">Index entries for sequences computed from exponents in factorization of n</a>.
%t A402676 q[k_] := Length[Union[Select[FactorInteger[k][[;; , 2]], EvenQ]]] == 1; Select[Range[210], q]
%o A402676 (PARI) isok(k) = #Set(select(x -> !(x%2), factor(k)[, 2])) == 1;
%Y A402676 Subsequence of A072587.
%Y A402676 Subsequences: A375031, A377816, A384519.
